# How many people still live without electricity?
subtitle: "Guess how many people still live without electricity, then a second question: where they live, and the country that switched on 420 million."
tags: ["geography","economics","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Still in the dark: how many?\" note \"1 in ?\""

## How many people still live without electricity?
sources:
    - id: owid_num
      title: Number of people with and without electricity access
      authors: Our World in Data, from World Bank (2026)
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/number-of-people-with-and-without-electricity-access
      finding: about 657 million people (≈ 660 M) lacked electricity in 2024, down from 1.34 billion in 2000; people with access rose from 4.82 to 7.48 billion
    - id: owid_region
      title: Number of people without access to electricity, by region
      authors: Our World in Data, from World Bank (2026)
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/number-without-electricity-by-region
      finding: '2024: Sub-Saharan Africa 579 million; Nigeria 87 million, DR Congo 85 million, Ethiopia 57 million; India 420 million in 2000, about 1.5 million in 2024'

