    icon ng size 200 set twemoji x 300 y 440 icon_look picture of "flag nigeria" hidden true
    icon cd size 200 set twemoji x 700 y 440 icon_look picture of "flag congo kinshasa" hidden true
    text ng_n "87 million" #b5482e cites ["owid_region"] x 300 y 290 font_size 52 hidden true
    text cd_n "85 million" #b5482e cites ["owid_region"] x 700 y 290 font_size 52 hidden true

    card title "How many still have no electricity?"

How many people in the world still live without electricity at home: no light switch, no socket to charge a phone?
    draw bulb dark

    ask "Click on the line where you think it is." on dark store g default "1500"
        right: Close: you said {g}, and it is about {g.true}.
        wrong: You said {g}. It is about {g.true}.

That is about one person in every twelve on Earth.
    highlight dark_answer

But in 2000 it was about one point three billion, twice as many.
    draw dark_marker_1 halv halved

    erase bulb

So the number in the dark halved, even while the world added two billion people.
    draw pop

    erase pop

    quiz "Where do most of the 660 million live today?"
        right: Sub-Saharan Africa: about five hundred and eighty million people, nearly nine in ten of all those without power.
        wrong: Think of where the grid has grown slowest, not where the most people live.
        * India and South Asia
        + Sub-Saharan Africa
        * Latin America

    erase dark dark_answer dark_marker_1 halv halved

    draw afr afr_l afr_n

    pause 1.5

    erase afr afr_l afr_n

If you guessed India, you would have been right in 2000, when four hundred and twenty million Indians had no electricity.
    draw india base bar00 l00

By 2024, India had connected almost everyone.
    draw bar24 l24

    erase india base bar00 l00 bar24 l24

Now the longest waits are in Nigeria and the Democratic Republic of the Congo, with more than eighty million each.
    draw ng ng_n cd cd_n

    erase ng ng_n cd cd_n

So the last six hundred million are mostly an African story, and India shows how fast that can change.
    draw afr afr_l afr_n

